Technical evaluation means examining or testing software behavior and suitability,
not relying on a self-built installation for ordinary personal or business use.

These activities may use local computers or hosted development and CI systems
under your control or acting on your behalf. You may create source forks,
branches, patches and pull requests on GitHub for proposed contributions, and
share synthetic screenshots and necessary build/test artifacts through those
contribution workflows. Artifact sharing is for verification, not app releases
or distribution to end users. Preserve copyright, license and attribution notices.
Use only data and services you are authorized to use; contribution examples and
shared evidence must use synthetic data and contain no private support records.

Except for the permissions above, incorporating Project material into another
product, distributing app binaries or derivative products, or operating a service
